---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · Simon Richardson"
  description="What the forms on this website collect, why, and what happens to it."
>
  <main id="main" class="marketing m-page">
    <div class="container privacy">
      <h1 class="m-heading">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="m-lede">The short version: the forms send your details to me so I can reply, and that's it.</p>

      <h2>What the forms collect</h2>
      <p>
        Your name and email address, your business name and current website if you give them, and
        whatever you write in the message box. If you arrived from a tracked link, the name of that
        source is included too.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I collect it</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to your enquiry or send you the site review you asked for. I don't add you to a
        mailing list and I don't sell or share your details.
      </p>

      <h2>Who handles it</h2>
      <p>
        Form messages pass through Cloudflare and are delivered to my inbox by Resend, an email
        service. The website itself is hosted on GitHub Pages, which may keep standard server logs.
        If you message me on WhatsApp, WhatsApp's own privacy policy applies too.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Your message stays in my email for as long as it's useful for our conversation or any work we
        do together. Ask me to delete it at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>This site doesn't set cookies. It counts visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which doesn't use cookies or identify you.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete what I hold about you by emailing
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you're unhappy with how I've handled your
        data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy { max-width: 760px; }
  h2 { font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: 700; margin-block: 2rem 0.35rem; }
  p:not(.m-lede) { color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
